/-!
# Finite geography of real klt fourfold models over a birational base

Let `π : X ⟶ Z` be a projective birational morphism of normal projective complex varieties, with
`X` a `ℚ`-factorial fourfold and `K_X` a canonical divisor of `X`. Let `P` be a rational polytope
of boundaries: the real convex hull of finitely many effective `ℚ`-divisors `V` on `X`, each of
which makes `(X, V)` klt. Then there are finitely many birational contractions
`φ_j : X ⤏ Y_j` over `Z` (birational maps over `Z` extracting no prime divisor), with every `Y_j`
normal, projective and `ℚ`-factorial, such that every `B ∈ P` has one of them as a log minimal
model: the transformed pair `(Y_j, φ_j_* B)` is klt, and `(Y_j/Z, φ_j_* B)` is a log minimal
model of `(X/Z, B)`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.exists_finite_isRealLogMinimalModel_of_mem_convexHull`: the finite geography.

## Implementation notes

* The polytope is `convexHull ℝ (QDivisor.toRDivisor '' V)` for a finite set `V` of rational
  vertices; effectivity of its members follows from that of the vertices. Over a birational base
  the zero divisor is big, so the polytope's common big core is `0` and no core hypothesis
  appears.
* The log minimal model is `MMP.Fourfold.IsRealLogMinimalModel`: nef adjoint over `Z`,
  effective `q`-exceptional comparison on a common resolution, strictly positive comparison at
  every prime of `X` contracted on the model, and projectivity and `ℚ`-factoriality of the model.
  Since `φ_j` extracts no prime divisor, the model boundary is the strict transform
  `MMP.Mori.RationalMap.transformDivisor (φ j) B`, which the statement names.

## References

* [C. Birkar, *Existence of log canonical flips and a special LMMP*][BirkarLC]
-/

@[expose] public section

